  "what_this_settles": "The denominator. Thirty-one durable writes on runtime paths across twenty-two functions, and twelve more inside schema migrations. Before this the box's scope was a guess.",
  "what_this_does_not_settle": "The numerator, and static reading cannot supply it. Deciding which of the thirty-one a given kill fixture crosses means following calls through test helpers and through internal journal functions; an attempt to extract it by regex found nothing for one fixture that plainly does durable work, because its calls go through helpers. Reading each by hand would produce a number nobody could check, which is the same failure as counting test names.\\n\\nWhat would settle it: a #[cfg(test)] counter incremented at each of these thirty-one sites, with the crash fixtures asserting which they reached before dying. That turns the claim into a measurement, and it is roughly a day. Until then the honest statement is module-level coverage, which is what the acceptance ledger records.",
